      "value": "You can already stand, crouch, and go prone in vr. You can lay down on your back if you change the prone animation.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-10-06T18:07:42.486Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I was wondering if you could add Desktop crouching (more of a \"prone\" state, TBH) to non-FBT VR, and maybe clarify \"Standing/Sitting Play\". I often play the game in my chair, but turn on \"Standing\" anyways, because I don't want to look crouched, except when I do. Maybe even make laying down on back possible for non-FBT? A longshot that would require a serious overhaul of the game's IK/animation systems, but it seems possible.\n\nThe new states would be something like:\n-Standing\n-Crouching\n-Prone (down on stomach/crawling, similar to desktop crouch)\n-Laying (down on back, like you can do with FBT)\n",
